And just look at, you know,
what the CIA did in...

00:24:48.854 --> 00:24:50.088
You know, rigged election,

00:24:50.088 --> 00:24:52.090
well, the CIA used to
try to rig elections

00:24:52.090 --> 00:24:53.925
in South American countries

00:24:53.925 --> 00:24:57.028
to favor fascist dictators
over communist dictators,

00:24:57.028 --> 00:24:59.731
'cause they were friendlier to
American business interests,

00:24:59.731 --> 00:25:01.233
in those countries.

00:25:01.233 --> 00:25:03.835
And, you know, again, this
was all under the radar.

00:25:03.835 --> 00:25:05.971
No-one knew about it until,
you know, decades later,

00:25:05.971 --> 00:25:07.472
when it was exposed.

00:25:07.472 --> 00:25:11.109 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so, that's that
constructive conspiracism.

00:25:11.109 --> 00:25:12.344 align:start size:75% position:25%
You should be...
- It's almost

00:25:12.344 --> 00:25:14.446 align:start size:81% position:19%
as if things might
be going on now

00:25:14.446 --> 00:25:17.082 align:start size:94% position:6%
that we don't know
exactly what's happening.

00:25:17.082 --> 00:25:19.251 align:start size:84% position:16%
- I have no doubt this
is the case, right?

00:25:19.251 --> 00:25:20.986 align:start size:84% position:16%
And we won't know
for another 20 years,

00:25:20.986 --> 00:25:24.856
somebody does a Freedom of
Information Act, you know,

00:25:24.856 --> 00:25:27.826
FOIA request, and finds
out, "Oh my God, in 2022,

00:25:27.826 --> 00:25:30.328
you know what the CDC,
or whoever, was up to?"

00:25:30.328 --> 00:25:31.596
"Oh, okay."

00:25:31.596 --> 00:25:33.598
(chuckling) "No, I
didn't know that."

00:25:33.598 --> 00:25:35.367 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Where do you
think social media,

00:25:35.367 --> 00:25:37.269 align:start size:94% position:6%
or how do you think
social media plays a part,

00:25:37.269 --> 00:25:38.203
in all of this?

00:25:38.203 --> 00:25:39.704
You know, one of the things,

00:25:39.704 --> 00:25:41.139
just in terms of the way
the internet's structured,

00:25:41.139 --> 00:25:42.274
that I always think about, is,

00:25:42.274 --> 00:25:44.109 align:start size:88% position:13%
I remember the internet
when it started,

00:25:44.109 --> 00:25:46.344 align:start size:84% position:16%
or, you know,
started on basic AOL,

00:25:46.344 --> 00:25:47.612
or Prodigy, or something,

00:25:47.612 --> 00:25:49.147
you'd go to a website,

00:25:49.147 --> 00:25:51.249
you'd get to the bottom of
the page, and that was it.

00:25:51.249 --> 00:25:53.251 align:start size:97% position:3%
Meaning, you could scroll
for a certain period of time,

00:25:53.251 --> 00:25:54.185
then it would stop.

00:25:54.185 --> 00:25:55.587
Then we got infinite scroll.

00:25:55.587 --> 00:25:57.522 align:start size:84% position:16%
So, more and more
and more kept coming.

00:25:57.522 --> 00:25:59.691
If you're on Twitter, you can
go more, and more and more.

00:25:59.691 --> 00:26:02.861
That rabbit-hole
is endless, now,

00:26:02.861 --> 00:26:04.462
and I think a lot
of that, probably,

00:26:04.462 --> 00:26:06.331 align:start size:84% position:16%
also feeds a certain
part of the brain

00:26:06.331 --> 00:26:08.633
that would lead people
to some of these ideas.

00:26:08.633 --> 00:26:09.901
- Yeah, it does.

00:26:09.901 --> 00:26:11.369
I mean the history
of conspiracism,

00:26:11.369 --> 00:26:12.871
there's always been
conspiracy theories,

00:26:12.871 --> 00:26:14.105
nothing new there,

00:26:14.105 --> 00:26:17.108
but, but the spread
of them in real-time,

00:26:17.108 --> 00:26:18.977
and the depth that
people could go.

00:26:18.977 --> 00:26:19.978
I talk about it in the book,

00:26:19.978 --> 00:26:22.147
of the JFK conspiracy theorists,

00:26:22.147 --> 00:26:23.582
you know, back in
the '60s, '70s,

00:26:23.582 --> 00:26:25.550 align:start size:97% position:3%
they're just meeting in
little hotel conference-rooms,

00:26:25.550 --> 00:26:27.052
with two dozen people,

00:26:27.052 --> 00:26:28.820
and they had their little
mimeographed newsletters

00:26:28.820 --> 00:26:30.655
that they'd mail out,
(chuckling) you know?

00:26:30.655 --> 00:26:33.758
And so, not very many people,
you know, knew about this,

00:26:33.758 --> 00:26:35.260
or were into it.

00:26:35.260 --> 00:26:37.829
Now you can reach, you
know, millions of people,

00:26:37.829 --> 00:26:39.297
instantly, in real-time,

00:26:39.297 --> 00:26:41.933
and so the spread is more rapid.

00:26:41.933 --> 00:26:44.603 align:start size:97% position:3%
The, you know, kind of,
going down the rabbit-hole,

00:26:44.603 --> 00:26:49.274
the siloing off of people
into these communities,

00:26:49.274 --> 00:26:51.409
that it's hard to penetrate,

00:26:51.409 --> 00:26:53.778
you know, that's
the harder part.

00:26:53.778 --> 00:26:55.046
- Is it, do you think,

00:26:55.046 --> 00:26:57.115
also easier to debunk
some of these things,

00:26:57.115 --> 00:26:58.550 align:start size:84% position:16%
because of the speed
of information?

00:26:58.550 --> 00:27:00.085
Just as fast as it can spread,

00:27:00.085 --> 00:27:02.187
it can also be debunked
that much more quickly?

00:27:02.187 --> 00:27:04.022
- Yeah, to me, that's
the only solution,

00:27:04.022 --> 00:27:06.291
is that, because I'm not
in favor of censorship,

00:27:06.291 --> 00:27:07.759
or kicking people
off of social media

00:27:07.759 --> 00:27:09.327
'cause they said
the wrong thing.

00:27:09.327 --> 00:27:10.862
This doesn't help,
for two reasons,

00:27:10.862 --> 00:27:12.731
one, you might be wrong,

00:27:12.731 --> 00:27:15.033 align:start size:97% position:3%
and that guy that you just
kicked off, he might be right.

00:27:15.033 --> 00:27:17.135 align:start size:84% position:16%
No one's omniscient,
how do you know?

00:27:17.135 --> 00:27:20.872 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, John Stewart
Mill, you know, it's like,

00:27:20.872 --> 00:27:23.308 align:start size:84% position:16%
if he who knows only
his own position

00:27:23.308 --> 00:27:24.576
doesn't even know that...

00:27:24.576 --> 00:27:26.478
So, it's good to listen
to these other people,

00:27:26.478 --> 00:27:29.781 align:start size:84% position:16%
and then second, if
you kick somebody off,

00:27:29.781 --> 00:27:31.316
cancel-culture, and so on,

00:27:31.316 --> 00:27:33.518 align:start size:88% position:13%
then outsiders
observing this will go,

00:27:33.518 --> 00:27:36.721
"Oh, I wonder if that guy
has something to say?"

00:27:36.721 --> 00:27:38.523
Because they're making such
a big deal about it, right?

00:27:38.523 --> 00:27:40.792 align:start position:0%
Banned in Boston: "Ooh, I
wanna read those banned books."

00:27:40.792 --> 00:27:41.760
- Right.

00:27:41.760 --> 00:27:42.594
(Michael chuckling)

00:27:42.594 --> 00:27:44.029
- And so, you know,

00:27:44.029 --> 00:27:46.197 align:start size:97% position:3%
when someone like Joe
Rogan has on Robert Malone,

00:27:46.197 --> 00:27:49.768 align:start size:84% position:16%
to talk about vaccines
and cardio issues,

00:27:49.768 --> 00:27:51.803
you know, everybody made
a big stink about that.

00:27:51.803 --> 00:27:53.304
It's like, well, first of all,

00:27:53.304 --> 00:27:56.074
Joe's not 60 Minutes, where
he has to have, you know,

00:27:56.074 --> 00:27:58.309 align:start position:0%
guests on each side, or
whatever, it's not what he does.

00:27:58.309 --> 00:27:59.811
You know that, going in.

00:28:01.012 --> 00:28:02.113
But if you make a
big deal about it,

00:28:02.113 --> 00:28:03.381
now everyone wants to know,

00:28:03.381 --> 00:28:04.783
"Well, who is this
Robert Malone guy,

00:28:04.783 --> 00:28:05.984
and what is his argument?"

00:28:05.984 --> 00:28:07.919 align:start size:84% position:16%
Because, no-one
seems to debunk it,

00:28:07.919 --> 00:28:09.688
they just say, "Oh, it
was bad he had him on."

00:28:09.688 --> 00:28:11.856
Well, okay, what is the problem?

00:28:11.856 --> 00:28:13.324
Somebody should say,

00:28:13.324 --> 00:28:15.193 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Here's the argument,
and here's the response."

00:28:15.193 --> 00:28:17.362 align:start size:97% position:3%
- And, what's so
interesting about that, is,

00:28:17.362 --> 00:28:18.596
if you remember,

00:28:18.596 --> 00:28:20.965
so he has Dr. Malone,
on who had, I think,

00:28:20.965 --> 00:28:22.167
if I'm not mistaken,

00:28:22.167 --> 00:28:24.669 align:start size:88% position:13%
more patents on mRNA
technology than anybody.

00:28:24.669 --> 00:28:25.770 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, it's not like
this guy's a kook, right?

00:28:25.770 --> 00:28:27.839 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Right.
- So he has him on,

00:28:27.839 --> 00:28:29.574
the media goes crazy about it,

00:28:29.574 --> 00:28:31.543 align:start size:84% position:16%
because he's talking
about Ivermectin,

00:28:31.543 --> 00:28:33.011
and all of these things,

00:28:33.011 --> 00:28:35.280 align:start position:0%
and then, you remember what
happened, about four days later,

00:28:35.280 --> 00:28:36.481
where, suddenly,

00:28:36.481 --> 00:28:39.417 align:start size:88% position:13%
we had a week of Joe
Rogan saying the N word,

00:28:39.417 --> 00:28:42.020 align:start size:94% position:6%
and should Joe Rogan be
de-platformed off Spotify,

00:28:42.020 --> 00:28:43.254
and everywhere else?

00:28:43.254 --> 00:28:45.857
And that, I think, led
people to believe...

00:28:45.857 --> 00:28:47.325
You know,

00:28:47.325 --> 00:28:48.827 align:start size:97% position:3%
I don't even know that this
is a conspiracy theory,

00:28:48.827 --> 00:28:51.463 align:start size:94% position:6%
but that there was some
sort of coordinated attack

00:28:51.463 --> 00:28:53.031
by the corporate press on Rogan.

00:28:53.031 --> 00:28:55.266 align:start size:84% position:16%
Like, he was becoming
too influential,

00:28:55.266 --> 00:28:57.235
so it behooved CNN

00:28:57.235 --> 00:29:01.039 align:start size:94% position:6%
to push these, "Oh, Joe
Rogan's a racist" stories,

00:29:01.039 --> 00:29:03.174 align:start size:84% position:16%
because he's moving
in on their territory.

00:29:03.174 --> 00:29:04.609 align:start size:84% position:16%
I don't know if
that's a conspiracy,

00:29:04.609 --> 00:29:07.946 align:start size:97% position:3%
I mean, I don't have the
documents from Zucker at CNN,

00:29:07.946 --> 00:29:09.414
(Michael chuckling)

00:29:09.414 --> 00:29:11.416 align:start size:97% position:3%
but it feels like something
that's, kind of, there.

00:29:11.416 --> 00:29:14.052
- I suspect that's not
a top-down conspiracy,

00:29:14.052 --> 00:29:15.487
like we think of a
conspiracy theory,

00:29:15.487 --> 00:29:18.356 align:start size:97% position:3%
of, you know, the Illuminati,
or somebody power...

00:29:18.356 --> 00:29:20.358 align:start size:88% position:13%
Cigarette-smoking people
behind closed doors,

00:29:20.358 --> 00:29:22.227
who're calling the shots.

00:29:22.227 --> 00:29:24.763 align:start size:97% position:3%
And the reason I'm skeptical
of most of those theories

00:29:24.763 --> 00:29:27.031 align:start size:84% position:16%
is because the world
is too complex,

00:29:27.031 --> 00:29:28.266
there's too much randomness,

00:29:28.266 --> 00:29:29.667 align:start size:84% position:16%
there's too much chaos
from the bottom up,

00:29:29.667 --> 00:29:31.402
and no one can control it.

00:29:31.402 --> 00:29:32.403
No one's in control.

00:29:32.403 --> 00:29:33.872
This is part of my theory,

00:29:33.872 --> 00:29:38.409
is that it's one thing
to be a little afraid,

00:29:38.409 --> 00:29:41.246 align:start size:88% position:13%
or anxious about there's
some cabal going on,

00:29:41.246 --> 00:29:43.414 align:start size:97% position:3%
of 12 people called the
Illuminati, running the world,

00:29:43.414 --> 00:29:45.216
and doing a crappy job of it.

00:29:45.216 --> 00:29:46.451
(both chuckling)

00:29:46.451 --> 00:29:47.585
But, it's quite
another to think,

00:29:47.585 --> 00:29:49.888
"Actually, nobody's in control."

00:29:49.888 --> 00:29:53.658 align:start position:0%
Right there, no one can explain
the economy, why wars...

00:29:53.658 --> 00:29:55.326 align:start size:84% position:16%
I mean, I don't think
Putin even knows

00:29:55.326 --> 00:29:56.961 align:start size:84% position:16%
if he's gonna use
tactical nukes or not,

00:29:56.961 --> 00:29:59.230
let alone Biden or the
Defense Department, or...

00:29:59.230 --> 00:30:00.598
I don't think anybody knows.

00:30:00.598 --> 00:30:02.934
It's just impossible to know.

00:30:02.934 --> 00:30:04.169 align:start size:88% position:13%
So, I think...
- Do you view that as...

00:30:04.169 --> 00:30:05.703
Is that scary, or
more comforting,

00:30:05.703 --> 00:30:07.038
if nobody's in control?

00:30:07.038 --> 00:30:09.474 align:start size:88% position:13%
- I like it, 'cause
I'm, kinda, libertarian,

00:30:09.474 --> 00:30:10.642
in my personal attitudes,

00:30:10.642 --> 00:30:12.277
and it's okay with me.

00:30:12.277 --> 00:30:16.681 align:start size:88% position:13%
But people that
prefer a structured,
hierarchical worldview,

00:30:16.681 --> 00:30:18.817
that's predictable, they're not.

00:30:18.817 --> 00:30:21.920 align:start size:84% position:16%
They tend to be
more conspiratorial,
in their thinking.

00:30:21.920 --> 00:30:23.354
A little more paranoid,

00:30:23.354 --> 00:30:26.191 align:start size:97% position:3%
a little more suspicious
that there's things going on.

00:30:26.191 --> 00:30:29.127
And again, things do go
on, so how do you know?

00:30:29.127 --> 00:30:31.596 align:start size:81% position:19%
Well, my little
test is, you know,

00:30:31.596 --> 00:30:33.932
the more people that have to
be involved in the conspiracy,

00:30:33.932 --> 00:30:36.201 align:start size:84% position:16%
the less likely
the theory is true.

00:30:36.201 --> 00:30:37.902
The more components that
have to come together,

00:30:37.902 --> 00:30:39.971
just at the right time
and the right place,

00:30:39.971 --> 00:30:41.472
again, it's probably not likely,

00:30:41.472 --> 00:30:44.375 align:start size:88% position:13%
if a lot of things have
to happen, because,

00:30:44.375 --> 00:30:47.045
again, chance, chaos,

00:30:47.045 --> 00:30:48.813 align:start size:84% position:16%
contingency,
accidents, you know?

00:30:48.813 --> 00:30:51.482
People just don't do what
they're supposed to do.

00:30:51.482 --> 00:30:53.918
You know, I remember that,
when my first book came out,

00:30:53.918 --> 00:30:56.888
I went on G. Gordon Liddy's
radio show, in Washington DC,

00:30:56.888 --> 00:30:58.389
"Why People Believe
Weird Things", so...

00:30:58.389 --> 00:31:00.225
I discussed conspiracies
a little bit in there,

00:31:00.225 --> 00:31:01.526 align:start size:84% position:16%
and he asked me
about it, and I said,

00:31:01.526 --> 00:31:03.428
"Well, you're the expert,

00:31:03.428 --> 00:31:05.330 align:start size:81% position:19%
(chuckling) you're
Mr. Watergate."

00:31:05.330 --> 00:31:06.931
And he says,

00:31:06.931 --> 00:31:10.034 align:start size:84% position:16%
"Well, actually, most
conspiracies are a
bunch of baloney,

00:31:10.034 --> 00:31:11.236
conspiracy theories are,

00:31:11.236 --> 00:31:12.904
because people can't
keep their mouths shut,

00:31:12.904 --> 00:31:14.739
and most people
are incompetent."

00:31:14.739 --> 00:31:17.876
And, you know, so this is
like 9/11 truth, you know,

00:31:17.876 --> 00:31:20.044 align:start size:88% position:13%
the Bush administration
was in on 9/11,

00:31:20.044 --> 00:31:21.613 align:start size:84% position:16%
let it happen on
purpose, (indistinct),

00:31:21.613 --> 00:31:24.249
or made it happen, on
purpose (indistinct).

00:31:24.249 --> 00:31:26.517 align:start size:81% position:19%
Well, in fact,
negative evidence,

00:31:26.517 --> 00:31:29.320 align:start size:97% position:3%
WikiLeaks, you know, millions
of classified documents,

00:31:29.320 --> 00:31:32.557 align:start size:84% position:16%
not one, not one
document about 9/11,

00:31:32.557 --> 00:31:34.525
or "We know they're coming",
or "We're gonna let it happen",

00:31:34.525 --> 00:31:35.994 align:start size:84% position:16%
or, you know,
planting explosive.

00:31:35.994 --> 00:31:37.262
Nothing, right?

00:31:37.262 --> 00:31:41.132
So, that tells me, if
it was an inside job,

00:31:41.132 --> 00:31:42.867 align:start size:84% position:16%
and these were
classified documents,

00:31:42.867 --> 00:31:45.270 align:start size:97% position:3%
we would predict that there
should be some leakage, there.

00:31:45.270 --> 00:31:46.838
There isn't.

00:31:46.838 --> 00:31:48.473
Because, most conspiracies, we
do find out about 'em, right?

00:31:48.473 --> 00:31:50.742 align:start size:88% position:13%
Lincoln was assassinated
by conspiracy.

00:31:50.742 --> 00:31:52.577
We knew within hours who did it.

00:31:52.577 --> 00:31:54.012
Same thing with Kennedy,

00:31:54.012 --> 00:31:55.146 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, Oswald was
discovered within an hour,

00:31:55.146 --> 00:31:57.248
they had him, at that theater.

00:31:57.248 --> 00:31:59.050
And so, we find out
about these things,

00:31:59.050 --> 00:32:01.085
but not one person wants
to go on record about,

00:32:01.085 --> 00:32:02.954
you know, the fake moon-landing,

00:32:02.954 --> 00:32:05.290
or 9/11 is an inside job, or...

00:32:05.290 --> 00:32:06.524
Not one.

00:32:06.524 --> 00:32:08.893 align:start size:81% position:19%
So, that's very
probably not true.

00:32:08.893 --> 00:32:10.395
- What would you say

00:32:10.395 --> 00:32:12.964
about something like the
Hunter Biden laptop story?

00:32:12.964 --> 00:32:14.799
Where, you know, New York Post,

00:32:14.799 --> 00:32:16.000
which is generally thought of

00:32:16.000 --> 00:32:17.602 align:start size:81% position:19%
as a reputable
news organization,

00:32:17.602 --> 00:32:19.871
they say "This is true."

00:32:19.871 --> 00:32:22.073 align:start size:88% position:13%
They, you know, they
have their sources, etc.

00:32:22.073 --> 00:32:24.609 align:start size:88% position:13%
Big tech Twitter,
particularly, comes in,

00:32:24.609 --> 00:32:25.843
you can't share these stories,

00:32:25.843 --> 00:32:27.078
you can't even share them

00:32:27.078 --> 00:32:28.646
through your own
private messaging,

00:32:28.646 --> 00:32:30.615 align:start size:94% position:6%
your own direct messaging
on our platform.

00:32:30.615 --> 00:32:33.785 align:start size:88% position:13%
Then other platforms
start doing it, as well.

00:32:33.785 --> 00:32:35.920 align:start size:84% position:16%
Of course, it all
turns out to be legit,

00:32:35.920 --> 00:32:38.723
and there's a lot of pretty,
pretty bad stuff, on there,

00:32:38.723 --> 00:32:39.958
some nasty stuff, on there.

00:32:39.958 --> 00:32:41.592
I think a lot of people

00:32:41.592 --> 00:32:44.896 align:start size:88% position:13%
see that as a
coordinated conspiracy,

00:32:44.896 --> 00:32:46.664
that, in essence,

00:32:46.664 --> 00:32:50.068
that thing was going to
be damaging to Joe Biden,

00:32:50.068 --> 00:32:51.669 align:start size:84% position:16%
they wanted Joe Biden
to be president,

00:32:51.669 --> 00:32:53.204
they wanted to be rid of Trump,

00:32:53.204 --> 00:32:55.606
we accept that big tech
can just get in, on this.

00:32:55.606 --> 00:32:56.441
Like, does that...

00:32:56.441 --> 00:32:57.675
Is that a conspiracy,

00:32:57.675 --> 00:32:59.010
or is that 'cause he...
- Yeah, interesting.

00:32:59.010 --> 00:33:00.244
- Yeah.

00:33:00.244 --> 00:33:01.746
- That's an interesting
example, 'cause, here,

00:33:01.746 --> 00:33:04.248
it would be a conspiracy
in the traditional sense,

00:33:04.248 --> 00:33:08.419 align:start size:94% position:6%
if, say, the news networks
called each other,

00:33:08.419 --> 00:33:11.189
and said, you know, "I'm
not gonna run this story.

00:33:11.189 --> 00:33:12.457
Are you gonna run the story?"

00:33:12.457 --> 00:33:14.625
"I won't run it if
you won't run it."

00:33:14.625 --> 00:33:16.094
If that was shown,

00:33:16.094 --> 00:33:19.197 align:start position:0%
that would be a more traditional
definition of a conspiracy.

00:33:19.197 --> 00:33:22.200 align:start size:97% position:3%
More likely, is, it's more
of, kind of, a cultural shift,

00:33:22.200 --> 00:33:23.468
or trend.

00:33:23.468 --> 00:33:25.169
We're all liberals, we
wanna protect our guy,

00:33:25.169 --> 00:33:27.472
and so, we're just
gonna bury the story.

00:33:27.472 --> 00:33:28.873
I'm gonna do it,
you're gonna do it.

00:33:28.873 --> 00:33:30.708
It's, kind of, common knowledge.

00:33:30.708 --> 00:33:32.377
I don't have to call you up,

00:33:32.377 --> 00:33:33.811
you just know that, you know,

00:33:33.811 --> 00:33:35.380 align:start size:84% position:16%
we're gonna, kinda,
work together,

00:33:35.380 --> 00:33:38.883
to support our guy, or
criticize the other guy,

00:33:38.883 --> 00:33:40.385
that's more normal.

00:33:40.385 --> 00:33:42.220
That happens, I think, a lot,

00:33:43.087 --> 00:33:46.257
without the concerted, top-down,

00:33:46.257 --> 00:33:47.592
you know, private phone-calls,

00:33:47.592 --> 00:33:50.228
kind of, messaging, to
coordinate the effort.

00:33:50.228 --> 00:33:53.131 align:start size:88% position:13%
That would be my
suspicion, for that one.

00:33:53.131 --> 00:33:57.035
- You know, when, when Alex
Jones was banned, after...

00:33:57.035 --> 00:33:58.636
Was he banned after Sandy Hook,

00:33:58.636 --> 00:34:00.138
